l affair or two  hundred  thousand  with such an extensive list it seems we  should start at the very beginning  according to hesiod zeus had seven wives  and the first of these was not actually  hera it was metis  metis was the one who supplied a young  zeus with the special potion that caused  cronus to throw up and release all of  zeus's siblings who had been swallowed  and how did zeus repay metis for this  favor well he swallowed her whole gaia  and uranus had prophesied the son of  zeus and metis would one day dethrone  zeus and so having seen the same plan  fail for his father cronus he decided to  do the exact same thing  zeus and metis did however have one  child whom i'm sure you're familiar with  athena was born from zeus's forehead as  a regular birth wasn't possible given  zeus had eaten her mother  his second wife was themis the titan  goddess of law and justice from this  union came the hurai and the morai also  known as the seasons and the fates  wife number three was uranomi another  oceanid who bore the charities three  goddesses also known as the graces the  fourth wife was demeter who bore zeus a  daughter we know as persephone the fifth  wife was nemesin the titan goddess of  memory from this union came the nine  muses wife number six was lito who had  to flee to the island of delos to give  birth to artemis and apollo the last of  the seven wives according to hesiod was  hera the queen of the gods  with the wives out of the way we can  move on to the many affairs and  mistresses  now i am gonna warn you these stories  are weird  very weird  let's begin with the story of dana the  mother of perseus  dana was the daughter of king acrysius  the ruler of argos  the king was extremely frustrated by his  lack of a male heir and so he decided to  seek out the oracle of delphi to inquire  whether he would have a change in  fortune  the answer was a resounding no but she  did tell him that his daughter dana  would have a son she also told him this  son 